    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nInstall with lazy.nvim `{ 'echasnovski/mini.nvim', version = '*' },`  means the global `MiniFiles` fails to be created.\nInstall with lazy.nvim `{ 'echasnovski/mini.nvim', version = false },`  means the global `MiniFiles` fails to be created.\n\nIn above 2 cases 3 other globals are created  MiniAI, MiniSatusLine, MiniSurround are created.\n\nIve tried nvim 0.10 and 0.11 same behavior.\nIf I add `opts = {}` to the config MiniFiles global gets created.\n\nInstall with lazy.nvim `{ 'echasnovski/mini.nvim', version = '*', opts = {} },` works fine.\n\n\nI am under Debian 12 doing this.\nMy v0.11 install is an appImage.\nmy v0.10 is a brew linux install.\n\nSorry another issue i created recently somehow landed in v1 of this post. Removed now.\n",
