        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1697#issuecomment-2747416899) describes the core of the issue here.\n\nThe reason there is no `opts = {}` or `config = {}` in the 'folke/lazy.nvim' instructions is to make it more equal across all installation methods *while* there is an explicit note below instructions of every module (that needs it): \"**Important**: don't forget to call require('mini.xxx').setup() to enable its functionality.\". The fact that 'lazy.nvim' does that automatically under certain conditions is a bit too magical for my taste, so I'd rather suggest the same way of adding an explicit `require('mini.xxx').setup()` call.",
